      "lineNbr": 3416,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T16:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should we have a typed version of this (and only have a typed version of this, since it is private)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3416,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3416,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "022e3be4_87a54940",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3416,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T17:38:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is @hide and only used in Bundle, where we don\u0027t have domain knowledge of types and have to handle generic objects, so we\u0027d just pass null and it would be type-erased to Object anyway. Also, to make this really type-safe we\u0027d have to separate lazy vs non-lazy because you can expect a parcelable T but receive a Supplier\u003cT\u003e for the lazy value. Since this is only used in bundle, I\u0027m not sure it justifies the trouble now, at least not in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "4722d862_76ba3309",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3416,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 3416,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "966ab518_3f591548",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3561,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T16:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If \u0027T\u0027 is Integer, then \u0027type\u0027 may actually be VAL_PARCELABLE, and we will still try to unparcel the parcelable. Technically, we could know here to stop work, but in the current situation, we still try to read the parcelable. This means, we rely on partially reading the parcelable (reading the classloader), and we\u0027ll get an error there.\n\nHowever, what I\u0027m concerned about is the \"clazz \u003d\u003d null\" case (which represents a lot of existing code), if we could stop here earlier, we could prevent situations where we expect to read an integer value, but there is actually a parcelable. However, it seems now, if someone is trying to read an integer, they\u0027ll pass \u0027null\u0027 as a clazz. What they want is \"don\u0027t allow any class to be read\", but what they\u0027ll get is \"allow any parcelable to be read\".",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3561,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 3561,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2970e3a5dd56dd6a10f61f66b853c4de1698c2b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f895a9dd_a049db0b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 3561,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-29T17:38:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point on stopping early. I actually suggested this before :P (https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1832336/9..15/core/java/android/os/Parcel.java#b3638). We can do:\n\n  clazz \u003d (clazz !\u003d null) ? clazz.asSubclass(Parcelable.class) : null;\n  \nbefore calling readParcelableInternal().\n\nclazz \u003d null doesn\u0027t mean \"don\u0027t allow any class to be read\", it means don\u0027t perform any class check. Hao, can you make this clear in the javadoc of the internal methods that accept clazz \u003d null? Also, I added comments to the public APIs to call Objects.requireNonNull(clazz) before calling into the internal methods.",
      "parentUuid": "966ab518_3f591548",
